PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED. The mechanical half of declaring the governed faces in
the SHIPPED bundle layer (`cordis.patch.yml`), shown so the size of the change
is visible. READ THE LAST PARAGRAPH: on today's tree this patch is INERT — it
adds a provider the shipped row never consults, because the row has no
enablement key that does not fork with the provided service.

Two files, three hunks, ~20 added lines. Everything else the exemplar needs
(the v4 blueprint with `memberIoCeilings`, the Member preset row, the
declaration) already exists in `../exemplar/governed-member-preset.patch.yml`
and is a product-design change, not a wiring change.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ exports
   ".": "./packages/client/composition-shim/index.js",
   "./host": "./packages/runtime/dist/packages/runtime/src/plugin/host.js",
   "./spill-local": "./packages/runtime/dist/packages/runtime/src/plugin/team-spill-local.js",
+  "./governed-realm": "./packages/runtime/dist/packages/runtime/src/plugin/live/a5sf-governed-realm.mjs",
   "./client": "./packages/client/composition-shim/client-bundle.js",
   "./package.json": "./package.json"

--- a/cordis.patch.yml
+++ b/cordis.patch.yml
@@ -105,6 +105,15 @@
     - id: "team-spill-local"
       name: "dsh-agent-team/spill-local"
+    # The governed realm: provides `teamA5sfRealm`, which the host row above
+    # reads lazily. The Member preset that pairs with it must NOT mount
+    # `persistent-shell` (install would refuse with
+    # TERMINALS_DOUBLE_TERMINAL_REFUSED and the Member would not come up).
+    - id: "a5sf-governed-realm"
+      name: "dsh-agent-team/governed-realm"
+      config:
+        realmId: "a5sf-governed-member"
+        scratchRoot: !!js process.env.A5SF_GOVERNED_SCRATCH ?? '/tmp/a5sf-governed-realm'
+        blueprintSource: *governedBlueprint
+        memberPolicies: *governedDeclaration
     - id: "dsh-agent-team-client"
       name: "dsh-agent-team"

THE INERTNESS (the seam gap this proposal cannot close by itself):
`a5sfRealmConfigOf` (`packages/runtime/src/plugin/live/a5sf-realm-row.mjs#L323`)
answers `undefined` — and the mount is never attempted — unless the TEAM row
carries one of `a5sfEvidencePath`, `a5sfMemberPolicies`, `a5sfMemberAuthority`.
All three are wrong here:
  - `a5sfEvidencePath` is a FILE PATH, and this layer's own header forbids
    machine paths ("Machine-agnostic by contract ... no machine paths").
  - `a5sfMemberPolicies` / `a5sfMemberAuthority` both set `config.memberPolicies`
    on the row, and a row with BOTH a declaration and a provided
    `teamA5sfRealm` throws (`two compiled-realm sources for one Member is
    ambiguous`).
So shipping the faces in this layer needs ONE small product change first: a
neutral enablement key (e.g. `a5sfGovernedRealm: true`) honoured by
`a5sfRealmConfigOf` and declared in `plugins/types.ts`. That is the smallest
real blocker, and it is OURS — not a pinned-host schema refusal. `CORE PATCH
BUDGET` stays 0 either way.
